Problem: Remove First and Last Position of Element in Sorted Array (LC 34)

Pattern: Binary Search (Boundary Search)

Approach:

Perform the first binary search to find the first occurrence.
If nums[mid] == target:
Save mid as first.
Continue searching left (right = mid - 1).
Reset left and right.
Perform the second binary search to find the last occurrence.
If nums[mid] == target:
Save mid as last.
Continue searching right (left = mid + 1).
Return {first, last}.

Time Complexity: O(log n) + O(log n) = O(log n)

Space Complexity: O(1)